course: dictionary
lesson: 10607
title: One word, many meanings: undone
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Undone can mean not tied, not finished, or, in old stories, ruined. Look at the words around it to find the right meaning. Is the sentence about laces, jobs or a change? Those clues tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Undone is the past participle of the verb undo. Undo means to unfasten or to reverse something. So «your lace is undone» means the lace has come untied, and «homework left undone» means the homework is not finished.
explain: «Most clues point to a few big ideas from the course: whether a change can be undone.» Here undone means cannot be reversed, put back the way it was. To check, swap in your meaning: «whether a change can be put back» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Undone means not fastened or tied, as in an undone shoelace, button or zip.
fact: Undone means not finished or not done, as in «homework left undone».
fact: On a computer, a change can be undone with the Undo button, which puts things back the way they were.
fact: In old stories, «undone» can mean ruined or defeated.
fact: The forms of undo are undo, undoes, undid, undone and undoing.
exercise: «Your lace is undone.» What does undone mean here? | Brand new and shiny | Finished and put away | *Not fastened or tied | Very long and thin
exercise: «Her homework was left undone.» What does undone mean? | Hidden under the bed | *Not finished | Torn into pieces | Finished very neatly
exercise: Which word is the past participle of undo? | undoes | undoing | *undone | undid
test: The Undo button lets you do what? | Make a new file | Make the screen bigger | *Put a change back the way it was | Turn the computer off
test: In a very old story, «undone» might mean what? | *Ruined or defeated | Lovely and bright | Lost in a shop | Very wet and muddy
exam: Which meaning fits «a change that can't be undone»? | Easy to fix with a button | Done twice | Very small | *Impossible to reverse
